\paragraph{Learned Code Verifiers.}
LEVER~\cite{ni2023lever} trains learned verifiers to rerank code generations by combining the program, its execution result, and the natural language specification---conceptually close to our classification formulation, though LEVER targets code generation reranking rather than repair verification and does not compare classification against generation-based simulation.
CodeT~\cite{chen2023codet} uses dual execution agreement between generated code and generated tests to select solutions without human-written tests.
Both methods verify code correctness via learned or execution-based signals; we extend this direction to repair verification and show that per-test binary classification suffices even at repository-level complexity where generation-based approaches collapse.

\paragraph{Classification vs.\ Generation in NLP.}

